# Patch 0074 — "Session only" clears the site's already-stored cookies, so its
# promise holds for them too (audit 2026-08-03; fixes patch 0049).
#
# Marking a site "Session only" set nsICookiePermission ACCESS_SESSION, which
# downgrades only cookies set AFTER the rule; cookies already stored keep their
# persistent expiry and survive the next quit. The UI note promised the site's
# cookies would not be kept after quitting — untrue for existing ones.
#
# FIX: when a rule becomes session-only (via the add row or the state menu),
# clear the site's currently-stored cookies with
# nsICookieManager.removeCookiesFromExactHost(host, "{}") — the same call the
# stock "clear cookies for this site" uses, across every origin-attributes
# partition. They re-set as session cookies on the next visit. The note now
# says cookies are cleared now and none kept after quit (and that a re-sign-in
# may be needed), matching the behaviour. Only the SESSION capability purges;
# Keep/Block do not.
#
# Marionette-verified on the built browser: _setCookieRule(SESSION) invokes the
# purge with the exact host; _setCookieRule(ALLOW) and (DENY) do not. (An
# end-to-end cookie-removal check could not seed a cookie — the test cookie
# store rejected API adds under cookieBehavior=5 — so the call-site spy is the
# verification; removeCookiesFromExactHost itself is Firefox's own stable API.)
